```rust
pub struct Note {
    pub id: u64,
    pub title: String,
    pub body: String,
    pub tags: Vec<String>,
    pub pinned: bool,
}

/// Returns notes whose `tags` contain exactly `tag` (case-sensitive, exact match).
/// Preserves the original relative order of the notes.
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|note| note.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```

**Key details:**
- `.iter().filter().collect()` naturally preserves the input slice's order.
- `note.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)` ensures an **exact match** (not substring). `String` implements `PartialEq<&str>`, so this works cleanly without allocation.
- The lifetime `'a` correctly ties the returned references to the input slice.

